.TH XPROXYCTL 8 "" "Xproxy" "System administration"
.nh
.ad l
.SH "NAME"
.PP
xproxyctl \- control and inspect a running xproxy
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.PP
\fBxproxyctl\fR [\fB\-socket\fR \fIPATH\fR] [\fB\-config\fR \fIPATH\fR] [\fB\-json\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [*ARGS*]
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
\fBxproxyctl\fR talks to the management socket of \fBxproxy\fR(8) and prints status, applies operations and follows logs. The user running it must be in the \fBxproxy\fR group (the socket is mode \fB0660\fR) or be root. Commands that need the configuration file (\fBvalidate\fR, \fBreload\fR, \fBtail\fR) read it locally; everything else goes through the socket.
.SH "OPTIONS"
.PP
.TS
allbox;
lbw(0.7i) lbx
lw(0.7i) lx.
T{
Option
T}	T{
Description
T}
T{
\fB\-\:socket\fR \fIPATH\fR
T}	T{
Management socket. Default \fB/\:run/\:xproxy/\:mgmt.\:sock\fR.
T}
T{
\fB\-\:config\fR \fIPATH\fR
T}	T{
Configuration file for \fBvalidate\fR,\: \fBreload\fR and \fBtail\fR. Default \fB/\:etc/\:xproxy/\:xproxy.\:yaml\fR.
T}
T{
\fB\-\:json\fR
T}	T{
Machine readable output for the status views (\fBstatus\fR,\: \fBstats\fR,\: \fBupstreams\fR,\: \fBquotas\fR,\: \fBwaf\fR,\: \fBsandbox\fR,\: \fBtls\fR,\: \fBseries\fR and the others).
T}
.TE
